// ICF codes, Socialstyrelsen inventory to SNOMED CT mappings, codes b5-b52
// Several sources map to the same target; each mapping is its own assertion.
context {
    collection "icf-snomed-ct" version="2026.1"
    source system="ICF" release="2026"
    target system="SNOMED_CT" release="20251130"
}
defaults {
    mappings {
        preference "primary"
        assessment-method "source-default-granularity"
    }
}
assessment "b5.omop" source="b5" outcome=no_match target-system="OMOP_EXT"
mapping "b510.1" source="b510" target="SNOMED_CT:111984006" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source b510 SNOMED CT 111984006 = ICF b510: the body functions of INGESTION — the functions
        involved in taking in food/nutrients through the mouth and processing them orally for
        swallowing, per WHO ICF definition, with children b5100 sucking, b5101 biting, b5102 chewing,
        b5103 manipulating food in the mouth, b5104 salivary secretion, b5105 swallowing, b5106
        regurgitation/vomiting. Target =, active RF2 production 20260701, the direct SNOMED CT observable
        that names ingestion (the taking in of substance). This is the closest standard equivalent;
        226320007 is the nutrient-specific correlate. Broader rather than exact: ICF b510 is a
        multi-child function block (b5100-b5106) bundling sucking, biting, chewing, oral manipulation,
        salivation, swallowing AND regurgitation/vomiting, where is a single observable for the
        ingestion act itself; the target names the central act but does not subsume the
        salivation/swallowing/regurgitation sub-functions, so it stands broader as the single best
        umbrella for the block, one level away in model framing (observable of the act vs ICF function
        block). High tier : direct term-and-scope match (ingestion = ingestion functions) verified
        active in the mirror, no independent Athena crosswalk re-verified.
        """
}
assessment "b510-b539.omop" source="b510-b539" outcome=no_match target-system="OMOP_EXT"
mapping "b5100.1" source="b5100" target="SNOMED_CT:90485000" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.87 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source b5100 SNOMED CT 90485000 = ICF b5100: the specific body function of SUCKING — the function
        of drawing liquid/nutrient into the mouth by creating a vacuum with the lips and tongue, per WHO
        ICF definition. Target =, active RF2 production 20260701, the direct SNOMED CT observable that
        names sucking. This is the closest standard equivalent; 45596005 is the reflex framing and
        55644006 is the non-nutritive behavior finding. Broader rather than exact: SNOMED CT models sucking
        as an OBSERVABLE (the measurable act) where ICF b5100 frames it as a FUNCTION (the physiological
        sucking mechanism), and the observable fully contains the source domain but is one level away in
        model framing. High tier : direct term-and-scope match (sucking = sucking function) verified
        active in the mirror, one-level-broader in model framing, no independent Athena crosswalk
        re-verified.
        """
}
mapping "b5101.1" source="b5101" target="SNOMED_CT:1202003" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source b5101 SNOMED CT 1202003 = ICF b5101: the specific body function of BITING — the function of
        closing the teeth/mandible to cut, grip, or break food (the incising/gripping component of oral
        food processing), per WHO ICF definition. No dedicated SNOMED CT or exists in the mirror: every
        biting hit (37298006 nail biting, 59901004 cheek biting, 69547003 aggressive biting,
        248069002/248072009 self-biting, 1303480003 unable to bite with denture) is a
        self-harm/behavior/problem finding, not the physiological ingestion-biting function. Target =,
        active RF2 production 20260701, the SNOMED CT observable that names mastication (chewing) — the
        parent oral-food-processing concept that subsumes biting as one of its components. Broader
        rather than exact/partial: biting is a sub-act of mastication (incising food prior to chewing),
        so mastication fully contains the source as an ancestor concept, but the target also subsumes
        chewing (b5102) the source does not name; the target is the legitimate parent. Low tier : the
        closest defensible target (mastication is the ingestion-food-processing parent), term-verified
        active, but a real semantic gap between the ICF framing and the SNOMED CT observable (no dedicated
        biting observable exists), and no independent crosswalk; recorded as the best available lead
        rather than a strong map.
        """
}
