mapping "b5106.1" source="b5106" target="SNOMED_CT:422400008" relationship=partial_overlap {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source b5106 SNOMED CT 422400008 = ICF b5106: the body functions of REGURGITATION OR VOMITING — the
        functions involved in the upward expulsion of stomach/esophageal/pharyngeal contents, per WHO
        ICF definition, with children b51060 vomiting and b51061 regurgitation. No SNOMED CT observable
        exists: SNOMED CT models vomiting as a DISORDER (422400008; the prior 15387003 disorder and
        139337005 finding were inactivated) and regurgitation as a FINDING (102622004; 78104003); the
        closest function observables (37811006; 80185009) name only a single-region mechanism, not the
        source's combined regurgitation+vomiting scope. Target =, active RF2 production 20260701, the
        active SNOMED CT concept that names vomiting. Partial rather than broader: the source bundles TWO
        distinct acts (regurgitation AND vomiting), and 422400008 covers only the vomiting axis — the
        regurgitation axis (b51061) is left uncovered, so a single target captures only one component of
        the multi-part source (the companion regurgitation target is the b51061 child map). Weak tier :
        the closest active concept, term-verified, but a real framing gap between the ICF framing and
        the SNOMED CT (a pathology, not a function), plus the partial coverage (one of two bundled acts);
        recorded to preserve a lead, not asserted as a mapping. mapping_type=partial.
        """
}
